- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/rasterizelayer.html
- Summary (EN): Rasterize Layer images a source layer as seen from the camera of another layer, producing a layer that shows the source from that viewpoint. It is the inverse of Project on Layer. Outputs are result, the source rasterized into camera_ref space, and depth, the distance from the camera to the source layer.
- Résumé (FR) : Ce nœud image un calque source tel qu'il est vu depuis la caméra d'un autre calque, et fournit aussi la distance de la source.

- Inputs meaning: ["camera_ref: supplies the camera viewpoint; its pixels are not used, only its resolution, location and viewpoint matter", "source: layer to image; must be Mono, UV, RGB or RGBA"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type the source input accepts", "Move to Origin: moves the output layers to canonical space", "Invert Transformation: inverts the computed transform used to project the source onto the camera reference", "Crop to Content: crops the output to the source's transformed data window", "Border: sampling outside the incoming layer boundaries, defaults to the layer border property", "Filter: sampling method, default Box"]

- Caveats: ["Re-cropping is not possible while Invert Transformation is on.", "The source input accepts only Mono, UV, RGB or RGBA layers.", "The pixel content of camera_ref is ignored."]

